<h2>Hashtable vs HashMap — complete comparison (exam table)</h2>
<p>Interview one-liner: &quot;Hashtable is legacy, synchronized, null-hostile, default capacity 11. HashMap is modern, unsynchronized, null-tolerant, default capacity 16. For thread-safe HashMap, use `Collections.synchronizedMap()` — don&#x27;t default to Hashtable.&quot;</p>
<h2>OCJP / SCJP exam rapid-fire Q&amp;A</h2>
<h2>What&#x27;s next (Video 150+)</h2>
